== Projects

=== Building Low-Cost High-Performance GPU Computing Servers for Laboratory
/Nov 2022 -- Apr 2023/

- Purchased and assembled hardware including motherboards, PSUs, RAM, GPUs, PCIe splitters, SSDs, and HDDs.
- Installed Xubuntu and configured CUDA, Docker, proxy rules, NAT traversal, and X11 forwarding.
- Set up a dataset server and shared directories with NFS.
- Created Dockerfiles for frequently used environments.
- Benchmarked combinations of CPU families, PCIe lane widths and generations, and NVIDIA GPUs.
- Tuned performance with htop, nvtop, iotop, top, bcache, and swap.

